  "notes": "Governmental funds modified cash basis; business-type funds accrual (as FY2023). Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement Total column (p5); Loan proceeds 230,000 printed under Other financing sources -> debt_proceeds. Business-type from the proprietary funds revenues/expenses statement Total column (p7, titled 'Statement of Net Position - Business-Type Funds'): receipts = operating revenues + interest income, disbursements = operating expenses + debt issuance costs + interest expense (= Statement of Activities business-type expenses 2,403,817, p2); transfers net = in 35,153 - out 500,202. Business-type Grant proceeds 28,259 (no grantor printed) left other / Grants. Governmental cash is printed only as separate lines (pooled cash, cash in bank, county treasurer, restricted cash/CDs), no single cash total, so beginning/ending cash are left null (as FY2023). Balance sheet from the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), lines tagged by column. Detail: General Fund from its combining schedule (pp13-14), one line per sub-fund column (Eliminations column of transfers 378,999 not recorded); the General Fund budgetary comparison schedule (p10) is not recorded (same totals, less detailed). Streets and Alley and Sales Tax Funds from their budget schedules (pp11-12); Streets intergovernmental left other state aid (no highway allocation printed). Utility funds have no supplementary schedules, so no business-type detail (as FY2023/FY2024). Business-type balance sheet p6 also prints due to other funds 95,903 within the funds (eliminated on p1). Read pages 1-14 of 14."
}
